<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Hebrew translation.

    The folder qualifier is "iw", not "he": Android matches resource folders
    against java.util.Locale#getLanguage(), which still returns the legacy code
    "iw" for Hebrew on every supported API level. res/xml/locales_config.xml uses
    the modern BCP-47 tag "he" because the platform locale picker parses that file
    with Locale#forLanguageTag; both resolve to this folder.

    Latin runs inside a Hebrew sentence (brand names, technical terms) are wrapped
    in U+2066 LEFT-TO-RIGHT ISOLATE / U+2069 POP DIRECTIONAL ISOLATE so the
    Unicode bidi algorithm cannot drag the surrounding punctuation to the wrong
    side. Runtime values are isolated in code instead; see ui/UiLogic.kt.

    Keys, plural categories, and format placeholders are kept in parity with
    res/values/strings.xml by LocaleParityTest.kt and tools/check_locale_parity.py.
-->
